       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **What was requested:** 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The maximum daily dose of metformin is 2,550 mg/day for adults. This order is three times that.\n- **Likely intent:** You may have meant 2,550 mg per day in total, which is 850 mg three times daily with meals.\n\nA dose this high risks severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n1. **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum dose).\n2. **A lower dose.** Metformin is usually started at 500 mg once or twice daily, or 850 mg once daily, with meals. It is then titrated up every 1\u20132 weeks as tolerated. This is often safer for a new start.\n3. **Something else.** Tell me the intended dose.\n\nPlease confirm with your supervising resident or attending as well. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
